  "verdict": "The bottleneck is Cu-Co, in every \u0394G branch of every live scenario. Its coupling is the two-state diabatisation (24b, t = 0.0015 eV): the crude \u0394SCF value (0.0013 eV) is half an energy difference of 9.4\u00d7 the SCF tolerance between two unconstrained solutions from one start, so it is not used (its table is kept as `scenarios_crude_dscf`). Every margin is a BRACKET over the sign of the computed 0.1299 eV site-energy gap and the \u03bb(Cu) reading (unsourced 2.0 \u22a5 cu_phen2 2.4 eV); \u0394G = 0 is the function's DEFAULT, not a measurement. The verdict is CONDITIONAL ON \u03bb(Co). At the assumed literature \u03bb(Co) 1.4 eV (no primary): \u00d70.018 \u2026 \u00d720.9 (\u00d71.8 at \u0394G = 0 on the unsourced reading). At the computed \u03bb(Co) 3.094 eV (computed \u2014 script 35 row `co_nh3` (ammine = the ZIF N-donor analogue)): \u00d74.1e-06 \u2026 \u00d70.0046 (\u00d70.00039 at \u0394G = 0). Turnover needs \u03bb(Co) \u2272 1.521 eV at \u0394G = 0 on the unsourced reading and \u2272 0.596 eV at the adverse corner. \u26a0\ufe0f The adverse corner is below turnover on BOTH \u03bb(Co) values \u2014 rate-limiting, not borderline. The \u03bb(Cu) bracket bounds the READINGS, not the site: both are unconstrained solution couples, and a framework-held Cu\u2013N4 node can sit below both. The Ru-swap reads \u00d75.5 \u2026 \u00d741 \u2014 across the \u03bb(Cu) reading only, on the borrowed Cu\u2013Co coupling, because no usable gap or coupling exists for the Cu-Ru (CHEM.32, Co\u2192Ru swap) node: 24d self-flags localised=False / physically_reasonable=False \u2014 the minimal cluster cannot form a clean Cu\u2194Ru diabatic pair, so its site-energy gap is not a measurement any more than its t_ij was; and its \u03bb(Ru) is a sum of Nelsen halves -0.256 and 1.037 eV \u2014 one negative \u2014 so that margin is indicative only."
